      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes and no. The lowp version happens to be identical, because the clamp against zero (that\u0027s semantically part of clamp_gamut, but not clamp_a) doesn\u0027t do anything, and is omitted here. In highp, clamp_a just clamps the high end, and clamp_gamut also clamps against zero.\n\nHowever: My next CL makes all of this confusion go away, because it turns out that we never use clamp_0, clamp_1, or clamp_a alone -- they\u0027re always paired. So I\u0027m going to collapse them down to two stages: clamp_01 and clamp_gamut (or maybe clamp_0a?). That will mean fewer stages that exist, fewer stages in pipelines, and no seemingly redundant stages like this.",
